# Drafted architecture

**Note**: This architecture is incomplete & for initial references. Its sole purpose is for initial generation of the final ARCHITECTURE.md file.
Agents will read ARCHITECTURE.md files for official instructions & planned architecture and will solely rely on that to implement

## Basics
The app should be a functional Learning Management System. Basics include:
- Account & Permission handling: 3 types of accounts 
  - Admin, Class Manager, Student. Each has their own features, frontend views, permission & data access
- Final product simulates 100 students, across 3 classes, 1 admin

## Admin
- Create & manage student, class manager accounts
- Create & manage classes: 
  - Set class's name
  - Starting & ending date (after that, the class is archived & students, class managers can no longer access & view class details & materials),
  - Assign class manager account to the class
  - define class's completion criteria
- Update timetable for classes, approve class manager's request for timetable changes
- Send announcements to selected classes/students

## Class manager
- Dashboard to view & manage students 
  - Student's info, 
  - Attended lessons 
  - Quiz results: points, time spent for each quiz
  - Course completion progress (marked by defined criteria for the class))
- Post & update course materials (slides, reference materials, ...)
- Create & manage quiz:
  - Add & edit questions
  - Set quiz deadline & duration
  - View quiz leaderboard, sorted by: names, points, time spent, pass/fail. Both ascending & descending. To reduce workload for the database, query & update results for every small window of time, real-time updating is not needed.
  - 2 types of quiz:
    - Test: Only 1 attempt, restrict tab-switching behavior during the test (count the amount of violations). Submissions are only allowed after 2/3 of duration passed. Class managers can allow the student to retake the test if needed.
	- Homework: Unlimited attempts. No passed-time restriction for submissions. No tab-switching restriction. Record all submissions & consider the attempt with highest point & lowest time spent as the final result.
  - In this MVP, only multiple choice questions with automated grading is supported
  - Create & manage session:
    - Assign a date to the session & wait for admin approval -> Timetable updates
	- Change assigned date & wait for admin approval -> Timetable updates
	- Generate attendance checking code for the session. Select/create post-session quiz
	- View student's photo proofs (an image including their face with the class's background) & approve attendance for the session
	- Post the session's videos so students who missed the class can watch
    - The class manager reserves the right to revoke/approve attendance status of any current/previous session.
  - Send announcements to students (can select which students receive the announcement)
  - Manage class's enrollment: Enroll/kick student from class, approve leaving requests from students)
  - Documents, videos should be stored on 3rd-party services because of limited hardware resources

## Students
- Homepage: View this week's timetable
- List of enrolled classes, find classes by name
- Class enrollment inbox: Shows an invitation if the class manager invites
- In each class:
  - Dashboard to view the class's progress: Track points, finished quiz, results, attended sessions, course completion progress, deadlines
  - View sessions: Attendance status (attended, awaiting approval, missed, watched session's video).
    **Note**: Watched session's video is a special state. It means the student missed the class, but watched the session's video online after the session & completed the post-session quiz
	Most of the time, it has the same value as approved, but is still categorized for transparancy
  - View quiz: Done quiz (with questions & answers if allowed by the class manager), available quiz, near deadline quiz
  - Access class's materials
  - Danger zone: Leave class. Need reason & approval from class manager before leaving